Give picotls-minicrypto's two chacha20 objects distinct names.

picotls-minicrypto compiles both the vendored cifra core,
deps/cifra/src/chacha20.c, and picotls' own ChaCha20 / ChaCha20-Poly1305
wrappers, lib/cifra/chacha20.c. Both become an archive member named
chacha20.c.o, so the static archive holds two members with one name. On
Apple platforms dsymutil then skips one of them ("skipping debug map object
with duplicate name") whenever the two members carry the same timestamp,
losing its debug information and emitting a warning for a -g link against
the archive.

The picotls wrapper is renamed to lib/cifra/minicrypto-chacha20.c, byte for
byte, and every build description that names it is updated: CMake, the
Visual Studio project and filters, and the Xcode project. The vendored cifra
file, the symbols, the flags and the behavior are unchanged.

Applies to picotls f06553b877ada93c860dd1db9002eabf7365292d, after 0001.

